Hi folks,

Excellent news: the wireguard-tools utility is now part of Homebrew, the
package manager for OS X. Now users simply need to type:

    $ brew install wireguard-tools

And they'll have the wg(8) tool. This tool implements the spec of [1] so
that it can configure crossplatform userspace implementations of WireGuard.

Regards,
Jason

[1] https://www.wireguard.io/xplatform/

